data.content:
It works. Here's the output:

```json
{
  "Name": "john",
  "Age": 30
}
```

The key piece is `JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase` — a built-in policy added in .NET 9. It converts the lowercase constructor parameter names (`name`, `age`) to PascalCase (`Name`, `Age`) during serialization. No custom naming policy needed.

The full program is at `PersonApp/Program.cs`:

```csharp
using System.Text.Json;

var person = new Person("john", 30);

var options = new JsonSerializerOptions
{
    PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase,
    WriteIndented = true
};

string json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(person, options);
Console.WriteLine(json);

public record Person(string name, int age);
```
